# Publish workflow (Gitea)

When you finish implementing requested changes to the Examinator software under `/opt/exam-simulator` (code, templates, static assets, docs, scripts, tests):

1. **Publish to Gitea by default** after the work is done, unless the user explicitly says not to (e.g. « sans publier », « ne pousse pas », « keep local only »).
2. Also publish immediately when the user asks with phrases like « publie », « pousse sur gitea », « mets à jour le dépôt », « sync repo ».
3. Use the helper script (reads the local token; never put the token in commits, chat, or remotes permanently):

```bash
cd /opt/exam-simulator
chmod +x scripts/publish_to_gitea.sh
./scripts/publish_to_gitea.sh "$(cat <<'EOF'
Concise commit message describing why the change was made.

EOF
)"
```

4. Follow the existing git safety rules: never update git config globally; do not commit `.env`, `venv/`, SQLite DB, or secrets; do not force-push unless the user explicitly asks.
5. After a successful publish, briefly tell the user that the Gitea repo was updated (branch `main` on `Aguilera_Lab/Examinator`).
6. Token file path (local only): `/root/.config/examinator/gitea_token`. If push fails due to auth, ask the user to renew the token there — do not invent credentials.
